{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZbSitZkUAYfBqf3oyzg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Conventions this repository already has:**\n- Error responses use `ApiError` envelope: `{ \"error\": { \"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\", \"fields\": [] } }`\n- Exceptions (ResourceNotFoundException, ConflictException) are thrown from controllers, caught centrally by GlobalExceptionHandler\n- ErrorCode enum is the machine-readable error identifier\n- Controllers fetch from repository, throw exception if not found or state conflict\n- Tests verify both HTTP status code and error body via MockMvc + jsonPath\n- Repository returns the persisted entity after save()\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt` — add ErrorCode for state conflict\n2. `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt` — add confirm endpoint  \n3. `sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — add tests for confirm scenarios\n\n**Risks:**\n- Need to add a new ErrorCode to the enum; existing clients won't expect it but it's additive\n- Idempotency requirement means confirming an already-CONFIRMED shipment must not throw, just return it\n- Must not break existing tests\n\n**Open questions:**\nNone identified that would change the correct behavior. The ticket is clear: CREATED→CONFIRMED, retries on CONFIRMED succeed silently, CANCELLED→409, missing→404.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt**: Add `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED` to ErrorCode enum. This error code will be used when attempting to confirm a shipment that is in an invalid state (CANCELLED).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` endpoint that:\n   - Fetches the shipment by shipmentId; throw ResourceNotFoundException if not found (404)\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, return it as-is (idempotent retry)\n   - If status is CREATED, update to CONFIRMED, save, return it (200)\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED code (409)\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add four test cases:\n   - Confirming a CREATED shipment transitions to CONFIRMED\n   - Confirming an already-CONFIRMED shipment succeeds and returns unchanged\n   - Confirming a CANCELLED shipment returns 409 with error envelope\n   - Confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404 with error envelope\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Instead of adding a new ErrorCode, reuse SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS or a generic VALIDATION_FAILED. Rejected because SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS is about duplicate IDs (not state), and VALIDATION_FAILED is for input validation, not state transitions. A specific code like SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED is clearer for clients to handle.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Response | Mechanism |\n|------|------|-------|----------|-----------|\n| CREATED → CONFIRMED | findById() | save(CONFIRMED) | 200 + shipment | Normal return |\n| CONFIRMED → CONFIRMED (retry) | findById() | — | 200 + shipment | Early return, no write |\n| CANCELLED → ? | findById() | — | 409 + error | ConflictException + GlobalExceptionHandler |\n| Missing ID | findById() returns null | — | 404 + error | ResourceNotFoundException + GlobalExceptionHandler |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n1. **Confirm CREATED** — create S-1, POST confirm, expect 200, verify status is CONFIRMED\n2. **Confirm already CONFIRMED** — create S-2, confirm once, confirm again, expect 200 both times, status unchanged\n3. **Confirm CANCELLED** — directly write CANCELLED shipment to repo (via repository access in test), POST confirm, expect 409 with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED code\n4. **Confirm missing** — POST confirm to non-existent ID, expect 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll write the code. First, I'll add the error code:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1197,"cache_read_input_tokens":16503,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1197},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0e52dfab-26c7-4c6f-b779-624192a7889e","uuid":"2f6111ed-ace5-4ac2-81a9-9686b2f6ac48","timestamp":"2026-09-30T12:06:29.932Z","request_id":"req_011CfZbSiWjuNLYHfzWMeRm7"}
